<figure class="identity" data-identity aria-labelledby="r39-identity-title">
 <p class="figure-title" id="r39-identity-title">Figure 1 · Which old row does the update mean?</p>
 <p>Anonymous scratch table: try to change row 1’s value from <code>before</code> to <code>after</code>.</p>
 <label>Replica identity <select data-identity-mode><option value="key">Primary key: row_no</option><option value="none">No identity</option><option value="full">FULL: entire old row</option></select></label>
 <div class="route">
  <div><strong>Publisher</strong><table><caption>Attempted source update</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Row</th><th scope="col"><code>row_no</code></th><th scope="col"><code>value</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Before</th><td>1</td><td><code>before</code></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Requested</th><td>1</td><td><code>after</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p data-source data-live>UPDATE allowed</p></div>
  <div class="message"><strong>Logical message</strong><p data-message data-live>Match the old row by its primary key.</p><dl><dt>Old row match</dt><dd><code data-match data-live>row_no = 1</code></dd><dt>New row values</dt><dd><code data-new-value data-live>value = after</code></dd></dl></div>
  <div><strong>Subscriber</strong><table><caption data-target data-live>Row after apply</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col"><code>row_no</code></th><th scope="col"><code>value</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><code data-target-value data-live>after</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
 </div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The primary key identifies the old row. The subscriber does not need the publisher’s physical page address.</p>
 <figcaption>A conceptual comparison, rather than a protocol packet capture. In the native drill, the source UPDATE failed without identity and succeeded after a primary key was added on both sides. The FULL case is documented behaviour, not an additional native test.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Read the three cases as text</summary><p>The old source row has row_no 1 and value before; the requested new row has row_no 1 and value after. Default identity matches old row_no 1, then changes value to after. Without an identity, an UPDATE on a table publishing updates fails on the publisher before it can become a usable stream change. The subscriber keeps row_no 1 and value before. FULL matches old row_no 1 and value before, then changes value to after, with more old data to send and datatype/index restrictions to consider.</p></details>
</figure>
<style>.identity{margin:2rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.55 var(--font-sans)}.identity .figure-title{margin:0 0 1rem;font-size:1.1rem}.route{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.5rem;margin:1rem 0}.route>div{padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);min-width:0}.route p{margin:.7rem 0 0}.route table{display:table;table-layout:auto;width:100%;overflow:visible;margin:.8rem 0;font-size:.82rem}.route caption{text-align:left;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:.3rem}.route th,.route td{padding:.35rem .15rem;white-space:nowrap;overflow-wrap:normal}.route code{padding:.1em;font-size:.9em}.message dl{margin:.8rem 0 0}.message dt{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.5rem}.message dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.route .message{border-color:var(--color-accent);border-style:dashed}select{max-width:100%;font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.4rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:1rem 0}details p{margin-top:.8rem}@media(max-width:600px){.route{grid-template-columns:1fr}.message:before{content:'↓ ';color:var(--color-accent)}}</style>
<script>
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-identity]')){
 const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-identity-mode]')!;
 const states={
  key:['UPDATE allowed','Match the old row by its primary key.','row_no = 1','value = after','Row after apply','after','The primary key identifies the old row. The subscriber does not need the publisher’s physical page address.'],
  none:['UPDATE refused; source value stays before','No update message is sent.','None: no replica identity','None: source UPDATE refused','Row unchanged','before','The table publishes updates but supplies no identity for the old row. PostgreSQL refuses this source UPDATE rather than guessing its target.'],
  full:['UPDATE allowed','Match all values from the old row.','row_no = 1; value = before','row_no = 1; value = after','Row after apply','after','FULL uses the whole old row as its identity. It can require more WAL and more matching work than a suitable key; supported datatypes and an appropriate subscriber index matter.']
 };
 select.addEventListener('change',()=>{const s=states[select.value as keyof typeof states];for(const [i,selector] of ['[data-source]','[data-message]','[data-match]','[data-new-value]','[data-target]','[data-target-value]','[data-explanation]'].entries())root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=s[i];});
}
</script>
